# Protocol rows on Android = the engines' own synthetic benchmarks: prefill forced to exactly 1024 tokens with no prompt, decode 256 (methodology/agreed-protocol-gemma4.md "The spec"); vendor rows, never pooled with the task-prompt long-context-1024-gen256 rows.
# LiteRT-LM = litert_lm_advanced_main --benchmark --benchmark_prefill_tokens=1024 --benchmark_decode_tokens=256 --max_num_tokens=2048 (context-tokens=2048; android/bench/run_cell.py engine_command), one cold process per run, one schema-v1 record per run.
# llama.cpp = llama-bench -p 1024 -n 256 -o json (no context flag: llama-bench sizes its own context, recorded as llama-bench-managed; repetitions and warmup are llama-bench's defaults), one launch per run, coldRun false.
# MLX has no Android arm; on Apple devices only LiteRT-LM has a forced-prefill entry (matrices/dashboard-protocol1024-v1.cells).
# Prepared 2026-10-06 (round m3 of the dashboard first-tab lane); same artifacts (file=), backends and cooldowns as the weekly set (matrices/dashboard-text-v1-android-*.cells); anchors = matrices/anchors.cells.


